retail = {{"No flying","Nothing flies but the flight paths, and you have to visit a flight master once before you can fly from it. Regular mounts come at level 40, fast ones at 60."},
{"No level scaling","Every zone, enemy and dungeon has its own level and keeps it. An enemy's number tells you how hard it is, and old zones stay easy."},
{"You go to the dungeon yourself","The group tool lists people looking for the same thing. It doesn't put a group together or take you there, and meeting stones do nothing. A warlock's Ritual of Summoning is the only summon. The Dungeons tab shows the way in."},
{"Spells are bought","New spells and better ranks come from your class trainer, for money, as you level. What now? lists what you can buy."},
{"Talent points, one a level","From level 10, in three trees, 51 in all at 60. The Talents tab has a plan for each way to play."},
{"Weapons are learned too","You start with a few kinds. The others are taught by weapon masters. See Class, Weapons & armor."},
{"Mail and plate come at 40","Hunters and shamans wear leather until 40, then mail; warriors and paladins mail until 40, then plate."},
{"Dying costs something","Run back to your body for free. The Spirit Healer brings you back on the spot, but your gear loses durability and you may be weakened for a while. Repair at vendors marked with an anvil."},
{"Two professions","Two main ones, plus Cooking, First Aid and Fishing for everybody. Recipes come from trainers, vendors, drops, reputations and Merchant's Favor: Professions, Find a recipe."},
{"Classic or Enhanced","The first time you log in the game asks. Enhanced turns on quest markers, one big bag, transmog and the new models. Change it any time in Options."},
{"The map shows your quests","M opens the world map with your quests and their areas (with markers on), L your quest log. Sunstone's route puts them in order."},
{"Rulesets","Normal, PvP, Roleplay and Roleplay-PvP, Hardcore later. You group, guild and raid only with your own faction on the same ruleset."},
{"Two names","A character has a main name and a second one; together they're unique in your region. The second can be hidden on nameplates in Options."},
{"Level 60 is the end","The cap is 60; nothing higher has been announced."},
{"Riding is expensive","Riding at 40 costs 100 gold and a fast mount's training at 60 costs 1,000 (Honored with your own faction takes 10% off). Start saving early: the Gold tab helps."},
{"Addons are different here","Retail addons need a Forever version, and addons are kept out of some things in combat."},
{"Rested experience","Time logged out in an inn or a city turns into extra experience from kills. Innkeepers also set your hearthstone."},
{"New to Forever","Legacy Points, campsites, Library Books, Merchant's Favor and a new race. See Forever's systems."}},
systems = {{"Legacy Points","INV_Misc_Coin_16",{{"What they are","Points your whole account earns from Legacy Challenges. Each character spends them in its own three trees for small perks. The window is on the Y key."},
{"When it starts","Your first point comes at level 25, or at 150 in a crafting profession."},
{"Class challenges","One point for each class at level 25, 45 and 60."},
{"Profession challenges","One each at 150, 225 and 300 in Alchemy, Blacksmithing, Enchanting, Engineering, Leatherworking and Tailoring."},
{"Other challenges","Dungeon boss sets (Novice, Experienced and Master Spelunker), raids, honor ranks and battleground reputation, exploring Azeroth, and a quest line that starts with An Earnest Proposition."},
{"Professions tree","Working Overtime (better chance to raise a skill), Bountiful Harvest (more scarce materials when gathering), Luremaster, Performance Bonus, Bartering (vendors cheaper), Master Chef, Dedicated Study."},
{"Adventure tree","Well Rested (more rested experience), Thrill of Adventure (health and mana on a kill), Field Medicine, Field Guide (camp things ready sooner), Talented (talent points start earlier), High Alert, Frequent Flier (flights half price and faster)."},
{"Resourcefulness tree","Gourmand (food lasts longer), The Quick and the Dead, Reinforce (less durability lost when you die), Diplomat (more reputation), Permanence (long buffs last longer), For Great Honor, Reagent Economy (class spells need no bought reagents)."},
{"How many you can spend","One guide gives 25 a tree and also 16 in all at launch. Guides disagree on this one: check the game."},
{"Rewards for your total","15: a toy rifle. 25: the Spectral Bear Cub pet. 40: a tabard. 55: the Spectral Bear mount. Claimed from Innkeeper Wiley in Ratchet. They count points earned, not spent."}}},
{"Campsites","Spell_Fire_Fire",{{"What they are","A campfire you build in the world, with camp objects from professions around it. Rest a minute there and you get its buffs; other players can share it."},
{"What you need","Cooking, and Flint and Tinder. Basic campfire: Cooking 1 and Simple Wood, room for 3 objects. Journeyman: Cooking 90 (one guide says 140) and Star Wood, 5 objects. Expert: learned at Cooking 200, used at 220, Thick Logs, 10 objects."},
{"How long","A fire burns about ten minutes and is used up. Each character can put down one camp object, again after an hour."},
{"What they give","Roughly the class buffs, a little weaker, and they don't add to them: health (First Aid Kit), strength (Sharpening Wheel), intellect (Incense Candle), spirit (Faction Banner), attack power (Lodestone), crit (Camp Chair), mana (Mana Well), experience (Camp Tent)."},
{"Useful ones","Engineering's Repair Bot repairs and its Reagent Bot sells reagents; Leatherworking helps track beasts; Herbalism and Mining can grow nodes; Fishing has lures."},
{"Sleeping bag","A quest line across several zones gives a Cozy Sleeping Bag: well rested on top of the camp's buffs."},
{"Everything for it","Quests tab, Your campsite: the bedroll's chain with its map, every profession's camp objects and where their blueprints drop."}}},
{"Merchant's Favor","INV_Misc_Bag_10",{{"What it is","A currency from your faction's supply hub, spent on profession recipes and more (a guide lists the Pack Kodo mount at 6,000)."},
{"How to get it","Deliver what the hub asks for. Recipes that cost it say how much: Professions, Find a recipe, From: Merchant's Favor."}}},
{"Library Books","INV_Misc_Book_09",{{"What they are","Books found around the world, handed in for rewards by how many you've given. Factions, Library Books has the tiers and what each pays."}}},
{"Honor","INV_BannerPVP_02",{{"What it is","Earned fighting other players, spent on gear. Factions, Honor shows what it buys and what it would take."}}},
{"Raids","INV_Misc_Head_Dragon_01",{{"The first ones","Barrow Deeps (10 players) and Hyjal Summit (20), announced for 9 December 2026, and Onyxia's Lair. Dungeons tab, Raids."}}}},
